{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\qc\b\f0\fs36 Deployment Submission\par\b0\fs24\par\pard\left\qj\fs22 Activity description:\line In this activity, each student creates and deploys a basic web application using a cloud platform to learn real-world cloud concepts. The project should demonstrate deployment, internet accessibility, and basic resource management (compute and storage).\par\line Student:\line Siddharth Herma\line Enrollment: 240905041009\par\line Repository:\line https://github.com/sidherma/cloudtrip\par\line Pages URL (replace after deployment):\line https://sidherma.github.io/cloudtrip\par\line Files to submit:\line - Source code: index.html, style.css, script.js (in repository)\line - Deployment report (this document)\line - Screenshot of the running application (live site)\line - Optional: ZIP of the source-code repository\par\line Required screenshot:\line Open the live Pages URL in a browser and capture a screenshot of the homepage. Save as "live_site.png" and include it with this report.\par\line Deployment details to include:\line - Cloud platform used: GitHub Pages (static hosting)\line - Publish settings: Branch = main, Folder = /(root)\line - Build/deploy confirmation: GitHub Actions Pages workflow run (include screenshot)\par\line Submission checklist:\line [ ] Replace the Pages URL above with the actual URL shown in Settings → Pages after the workflow succeeds.\line [ ] Attach the live site screenshot (live_site.png).\line [ ] Attach the repository source ZIP (if required).\line [ ] Upload this DOCX and screenshots to the LMS (ALA).\par\line Notes:\line - This project is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. No virtual machine, backend API, or database was provisioned.\line - GitHub Pages serves static files over HTTPS and provides a public URL for the site.\par\line Contact:\line Student: Siddharth Herma\par\pard\qc\fs18 Generated by GitHub Copilot assistant\par}